Components are grouped in namespaces, imported from `svelte-pdf-mini`. Each page lists the namespace's anatomy, a live demo, usage and an API reference generated from the library's types.

| Namespace | Parts | For |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [Document](/components/document) | `Root`, `Loading`, `Error`, `Password` | Loading a PDF and its states |
| [Viewer](/components/viewer) | `Root`, `Viewport`, `Pages`, `Page`, `Canvas`, `TextLayer`, `LinkLayer`, `LinkPreview`, `Focus`, `BackButton` | Layout, rendering, links and navigation |
| [Zoom](/components/zoom) | `In`, `Out`, `Mode`, `Select` | Zoom controls |
| [PageNav](/components/page-nav) | `Prev`, `Next`, `Input` | Page controls |
| [Find](/components/find) | `Root`, `Input`, `Next`, `Prev`, `Toggle`, `Count`, `Result`, `Layer` | Search |
| [Outline](/components/outline) | `Root`, `Tree`, `Item` | PDF bookmarks |
| [Thumbnails](/components/thumbnails) | `Root`, `Item` | Page previews |
| [Minimap](/components/minimap) | `Root`, `Viewport`, `Markers` | A code-editor style overview |
| [Annotations](/components/annotations) | `Root`, `Layer`, `SelectionMenu`, `Popover`, `HoverCard`, `Margin`, `LineMarkers`, `List`, `Crop`, `Comment`, `Tool`, `Color`, `Undo`, `Redo` | Highlights, boxes, drawings and notes |
| [Paper](/components/paper) | `Root`, `Layer`, `Headings`, `CitationCard`, `CrossRefPreview`, `References`, `Figures` | Research-paper aids |
| [Toc](/components/toc) | `Tree`, `Flat`, `Breadcrumb`, `Progress`, `Rail` | Tables of contents |

## Common props

Every part that renders an element also accepts:

| Prop | Type | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ref` | `HTMLElement \| null` | The rendered element (bindable) |
| `child` | `Snippet<[{ props, …snippetProps }]>` | Render your own element; spread `props` on it |
| `children` | `Snippet<[snippetProps]>` | Content, receiving the part's snippet props |
| HTML attributes | — | `class`, `style`, `aria-*`, handlers… merged with the part's own |

These are not repeated in each API table.

<Callout>Roots that create state (<code>Find.Root</code>, <code>Annotations.Root</code>, <code>Paper.Root</code>) render no element: wrap the pages and the parts that use them.</Callout>
